WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.134 --> 00:00:17.519
The first month at Redmond College had seemed long, but the rest of the term went by quickly.

2
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:24.414
Before they realized how much time had gone by, Anne and all the Redmond students were facing their exams.

3
00:00:24.415 --> 00:00:31.587
When the results came back, the top places in first-year subjects were taken by Anne, Gilbert, and Philippa.

4
00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:36.810
Priscilla did very well, and Charlie scraped through respectably.

5
00:00:36.811 --> 00:00:39.552
After exams, came vacation.

6
00:00:39.553 --> 00:00:47.218
"I can't believe that this time tomorrow I'll be in Green Gables," said Anne to Philippa on the night before her departure.

7
00:00:47.219 --> 00:00:53.291
"But I shall be. And you, Phil, will be in Bolingbroke with Alec and Alonzo."

8
00:00:53.292 --> 00:00:59.637
"I'm longing to see them," admitted Philippa. "They really are such nice boys.

9
00:00:59.638 --> 00:01:05.196
And in Bolingbroke there'll be dances and parties and all kinds of fun.

10
00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:10.339
But I shall never forgive you, Queen Anne, for not coming home with me for the holidays."

11
00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:17.382
"I'm sure you'll forgive me. 'Never' lasts only three days with you, Phil!" joked Anne.

12
00:01:17.383 --> 00:01:22.217
"It was sweet of you to ask me and I'd love to go to Bolingbroke someday.

13
00:01:22.218 --> 00:01:27.295
I'd especially like to see the house where my parents lived and where I was born.

14
00:01:27.296 --> 00:01:32.681
But these holidays I must visit Green Gables."

15
00:01:32.682 --> 00:01:39.496
"You won't have a very good time," said Phil scornfully. "It sounds so boring there!"

16
00:01:39.497 --> 00:01:43.510
"In Avonlea?" said Anne, highly amused.

17
00:01:43.511 --> 00:01:49.498
"If you'd come with me to Bolingbroke," Phil insisted, "you'd have a wonderful time.

18
00:01:49.499 --> 00:01:58.568
People would go wild over you, Anne—your hair and your style and, oh, everything! You're so unique."

19
00:01:58.569 --> 00:02:03.882
"That sounds interesting, Phil, but picture this," Anne said.

20
00:02:03.883 --> 00:02:12.757
"I'm going home to an old country farmhouse, once green, rather faded now, set among some apple orchards.

21
00:02:12.758 --> 00:02:18.485
There's a stream nearby, and down the road is a wood with old fir trees.

22
00:02:18.486 --> 00:02:29.627
In the farmhouse there will be two middle-aged ladies: one tall and thin, one short and fat. They are Marilla and Mrs. Lynde.

23
00:02:29.628 --> 00:02:37.609
And there will be the twins, Dora and Davy—one a perfect model, the other what Mrs. Lynde calls a 'terror.'

24
00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:41.026
There will be a little room upstairs with an old feather bed,

25
00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:46.143
which will seem like heaven after sleeping on that hard mattress in the boardinghouse.

26
00:02:46.144 --> 00:02:49.025
How do you like my picture, Phil?"

27
00:02:49.026 --> 00:02:53.389
"It seems a very dull one," said Phil with a frown.

28
00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:59.441
"Oh, but I've left out one thing," said Anne softly.

29
00:02:59.442 --> 00:03:06.777
"There'll be love there, Phil—love like nowhere else in the world, tender love that's waiting for me.

30
00:03:06.778 --> 00:03:13.245
That makes my picture a masterpiece, doesn't it, even if the colors are not very bright?"

31
00:03:13.246 --> 00:03:17.014
Phil got up, went up to Anne, and hugged her.

32
00:03:17.015 --> 00:03:21.567
"Anne, I wish I were like you," she said soberly.

33
00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:25.861
The following evening Diana met Anne at the Avonlea station.

34
00:03:25.862 --> 00:03:31.650
As they drove up the lane, Anne saw that Green Gables had a very festive appearance.

35
00:03:31.651 --> 00:03:41.472
A candle burned in every window, and in the yard was a big bonfire with two little figures, Davy and Dora, dancing around it.

36
00:03:41.473 --> 00:03:46.631
"Davy was determined to make a bonfire for you," Diana told Anne.

37
00:03:46.632 --> 00:03:52.932
Anne got out of the buggy, and Davy hugged her tightly. Even Dora held her hand.

38
00:03:52.933 --> 00:03:56.629
"Isn't it a great bonfire, Anne?" asked Davy.

39
00:03:56.630 --> 00:04:04.165
"I'll poke it—see the sparks? I did it for you because I was so glad you were coming home."

40
00:04:04.166 --> 00:04:07.831
The kitchen door opened and Marilla greeted Anne.

41
00:04:07.832 --> 00:04:15.824
Marilla had a big smile, but not too big, since she had the old-fashioned belief that you should not show too much emotion.

42
00:04:15.825 --> 00:04:22.673
Mrs. Lynde was behind her, smiling warmly. They both hugged Anne and welcomed her home.

43
00:04:22.674 --> 00:04:26.488
This was the love Anne had described to Phil.

44
00:04:26.489 --> 00:04:30.982
A few days later, Anne met her old friend Jane Andrews.

45
00:04:30.983 --> 00:04:35.133
After they had caught up on each other's news, Jane grew silent.

46
00:04:35.134 --> 00:04:41.255
Then she turned to Anne. "I want to ask you something, Anne," she said solemnly.

47
00:04:41.256 --> 00:04:44.130
"What do you think of my brother Billy?"

48
00:04:44.131 --> 00:04:51.423
Anne gasped at this unexpected question. Goodness, what did she think of Billy Andrews?

49
00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:54.048
Anne had never thought anything about him.

50
00:04:54.049 --> 00:05:00.846
He was just the round-faced, perpetually smiling, not too smart, good-natured Billy Andrews.

51
00:05:00.847 --> 00:05:07.859
"I—I don't understand, Jane," Anne stammered. "What do you mean . . . exactly?"

52
00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.134
"Do you like Billy?" asked Jane bluntly.

53
00:05:11.135 --> 00:05:16.563
"Oh, uh—yes, I like him, of course," said Anne.

54
00:05:16.564 --> 00:05:23.508
Anne knew that she didn't dislike him. What exactly was Jane trying to say?

55
00:05:23.509 --> 00:05:28.085
"Would you like him for a husband?" asked Jane calmly.

56
00:05:28.086 --> 00:05:31.066
"A husband!" Anne exclaimed.

57
00:05:31.067 --> 00:05:37.683
"Billy wants to marry you," Jane explained. "He's always been crazy about you.

58
00:05:37.684 --> 00:05:42.039
But he was too shy to ask you himself, so he got me to do it.

59
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:48.652
I didn't want to ask you, but he insisted. Well, what do you think, Anne?"

60
00:05:48.653 --> 00:05:58.041
Was it a dream? Anne did not know whether she wanted to laugh or cry, but she could do neither, because she didn't want to hurt Jane's feelings.

61
00:05:58.042 --> 00:06:02.818
"I—I can't marry your brother, Jane," Anne said.

62
00:06:02.819 --> 00:06:06.707
"It never even occurred to me that Billy would ask!"

63
00:06:06.708 --> 00:06:12.036
"Well, think it over, Anne," said Jane. "Billy is a good fellow."

64
00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:17.237
"I'm sorry, I can't marry Billy," said Anne firmly.

65
00:06:17.238 --> 00:06:21.872
"Well, you've made your decision, Anne," replied Jane somewhat coldly.

66
00:06:21.873 --> 00:06:23.878
"And I hope you won't regret it.

67
00:06:23.879 --> 00:06:27.180
Billy is a good fellow, even if he is my brother.

68
00:06:27.181 --> 00:06:31.640
Anyway, he also likes Nettie Blewett, so he'll probably ask her."

69
00:06:31.641 --> 00:06:40.572
"Nettie Blewett!" Anne thought. After Jane had gone, Anne laughed but she also felt a hint of sadness.

70
00:06:40.573 --> 00:06:44.823
Anne had imagined that her first proposal would be very romantic,

71
00:06:44.824 --> 00:06:51.330
and that it would come from someone who was handsome, distinguished, and eloquent—her own Prince Charming.

72
00:06:51.331 --> 00:06:54.321
There was nothing romantic about this proposal!

73
00:06:54.322 --> 00:07:01.876
Billy Andrews had asked his sister to propose for him, and if Anne wouldn't marry him, he would ask Nettie Blewett instead.

74
00:07:01.877 --> 00:07:12.846
"Well, that ends my romantic dream," thought Anne sadly, "even if it was a bit girlish."
